    .intro h1{margin:0}
    .cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:16px;margin-top:18px}
    .card{background:var(--card);padding:18px;border-radius:12px;box-shadow:0 8px 24px rgba(12,12,12,0.06)}
    .card h3{margin-top:0}
    .cta-row{display:flex;gap:12px;margin-top:18px}
    button.alt{padding:10px 12px;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid #ddd;background:white;cursor:pointer}
    .planner-small{margin-top:18px;padding:14px;border-radius:10px;background:#f8f8ff}
    .list{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6}
    @media(max-width:940px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}.intro{flex-direction:column}}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <div style='font-weight:700'><a href='index.html' style='color:var(--mono);text-decoration:none'>Start</a></div>
    <nav>
      <a href='about.html'>The Clinician</a>
      <a href='specialties.html'>Offerings</a>
      <a href='approach.html'>Method</a>
      <a href='book.html'>Begin</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main class='wrap'>
    <section class='intro'>
      <div style='flex:1'>
        <h1>Areas of focus</h1>
        <p class='list'>I work with adults who are navigating sustained stress, relationship shifts, transitions (work, family, identity), and mood or worry that interrupts daily life. Below are common pathways clients ask for; each is shaped into tailored work rather than a fixed program.</p>
      </div>
      <aside style='width:320px'>
        <div class='planner-small card'>
          <h4 style='margin:0 0 8px'>Quick planner</h4>
          <label class='small'>Choose one focus</label>
          <select id='focusSelect' style='width:100%;padding:8px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid #eaeaea'>
            <option>Manage persistent worry</option>
            <option>Regulate low mood</option>
            <option>Navigate relationship change</option>
            <option>Transition support (job, family, move)</option>
            <option>Parenting support</option>
          </select>
          <div style='display:flex;gap:8px;margin-top:12px'>
            <button id='buildMini' class='alt'>Sketch plan</button>
            <button id='openBook' class='alt' onclick="location.href='book.html'">Book a consult</button>
          </div>
          <pre id='miniOut' style='margin-top:12px;background:#fff;padding:8px;border-radius:8px;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px'>Pick a focus and sketch a short plan.</pre>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class='cards'>
      <div class='card'>
        <h3>Regulation & mood</h3>
        <p class='list'>Work here centers on routines, small behavioral experiments, and noticing patterns that sustain low mood. We prioritize manageable steps and ways to re-engage with what matters to you.</p>
      </div>

      <div class='card'>
        <h3>Anxiety & persistent worry</h3>
        <p class='list'>Practical tools, attention to avoidance, and gradual exposure to difficult situations help reduce the hold of worry. The pace is collaborative—experiments are tailored to your tolerance.</p>
      </div>

      <div class='card'>
        <h3>Relationships & communication</h3>
        <p class='list'>We explore patterns of giving and receiving, boundaries, and clear ways to test new approaches. Therapy focuses on what you can change and how to do so without abrupt risk.</p>
      </div>

      <div class='card'>
        <h3>Transitions & identity</h3>
        <p class='list'>When life shifts—career, family, or identity—the work is about orienting, defining priorities, and settling into new rhythms with practical supports.</p>
      </div>

      <div class='card'>
        <h3>Short-form offerings</h3>
        <p class='list'>Named packages: Anchor Series (4 sessions), Deep Check (single extended session), Rhythm Care (monthly maintenance). Pricing is discussed transparently; I offer a limited number of sliding-scale slots.</p>
      </div>

      <div class='card'>
        <h3>Coordination & referrals</h3>
        <p class='list'>I collaborate with other professionals when helpful and will discuss coordination when requested. I do not provide emergency or forensic services.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div style='margin-top:22px;display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:center'>
      <button onclick="location.href='book.html'" style='padding:12px 16px;background:var(--accent);color:white;border-radius:10px;border:0;cursor:pointer'>Start with a consult</button>
      <a href='contact.html' style='color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none'>Questions by email</a>
    </div>
  </main>

  <script>
    document.getElementById('buildMini').addEventListener('click', ()=>{
      const focus = document.getElementById('focusSelect').value;
      const suggestions = {
        'Manage persistent worry': ['Weekly check-ins','2 small exposure tasks per week','Brief worry log'],'Regulate low mood': ['Behavioural activation plan','Daily 3-minute mood check','Short-term target: 4 weeks'],'Navigate relationship change': ['Define conversation goals','Practice one boundary script','Choose a small relational experiment'],'Transition support (job, family, move)': ['Set 3 concrete goals','Map support resources','Check-ins every 2 weeks'],'Parenting support': ['Identify one shift to test','Family routine focus','Coaching for challenging moments']
      };
      const plan = suggestions[focus] || [];
      const text = ['Focus: ' + focus,'Suggested structure:','- ' + plan.join('\n- ')].join('\n');
      document.getElementById('miniOut').textContent = text;
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>"} 
{"path":"approach.html","content":"<!doctype html>
<html lang='en'>
<head>
  <meta charset='utf-8'>
  <meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'>
  <title>How I Work — {{BUSINESS_NAME}}</title>
  <style>
    :root{--bg:#fbfbff;--muted:#5f6670;--accent:#2f7a5f;--card:#fff;--mono:#0b0b0b}
    body{margin:0;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:var(--mono);background:#fbfbff url('assets/img/pattern.svg') repeat}
    header{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:20px 28px}
    nav a{margin-left:14px;color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none}
    .container{max-width:1000px;margin:18px auto;padding:0 20px}
    .lead{background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(255,255,255,0.9),rgba(250,250,250,0.9));padding:18px;border-radius:12px}
    .columns{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 320px;gap:18px;margin-top:18px}
    .card{background:var(--card);padding:16px;border-radius:12px;box-shadow:0 10px 30px rgba(20,20,30,0.05)}
    .framework{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px}
    .pill{display:inline-block;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:18px;background:#f1f7f1;color:var(--accent);font-weight:600}
    .note{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}
    footer{max-width:1000px;margin:26px auto;padding:12px;color:var(--muted);font-size:13px}
    @media(max-width:880px){.columns{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <div><a href='index.html' style='font-weight:700;color:var(--mono);text-decoration:none'>Home</a></div>
    <nav>
      <a href='about.html'>Who I Am</a>
      <a href='specialties.html'>Offerings</a>
      <a href='approach.html'>Method</a>
      <a href='contact.html'>Connect</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main class='container'>
    <section class='lead card'>
      <h1>How the work unfolds</h1>
      <p class='note'>A relational, skills-oriented practice: I combine collaborative problem solving with short, practical experiments. Your priorities shape the plan. We check in often and adjust what isn’t useful.</p>
      <div style='margin-top:12px'><span class='pill'>Collaborative</span> <span class='pill' style='margin-left:8px'>Practical</span> <span class='pill' style='margin-left:8px'>Boundaried</span></div>
    </section>

    <div class='columns'>
      <section>
        <div class='card framework'>
          <div>
            <h3>Framework</h3>
            <ol>
              <li><strong>Clarify:</strong> We name one or two concrete goals and what success looks like in small, observable terms.</li>
              <li><strong>Experiment:</strong> We try short behavioral or cognitive experiments between sessions and look at results with curiosity.</li>
              <li><strong>Refine:</strong> We keep what helps, adjust what doesn’t, and build skills into daily life so gains sustain.</li>
            </ol>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3>Session rhythm</h3>
            <p class='note'>Most work starts weekly or biweekly. Some clients choose a short series (4–6 sessions) focused on a specific aim; others prefer ongoing rhythm. We discuss timing during a consult.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3>Boundaries & safety</h3>
            <p class='note'>I will discuss limits of confidentiality, expectations for session attendance, and procedures for cancellations. If safety concerns arise, we create a clear, immediate plan and connect with appropriate resources.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3>Who benefits</h3>
            <p class='note'>Adults motivated to try small, measurable changes and to reflect on how patterns operate in daily life. This work is not an emergency service and does not replace medical care when required.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class='card' style='margin-top:16px'>
          <h3>What to bring</h3>
          <p class='note'>A concise list: a short description of the concern, when it began, what has helped or not, and any practical constraints. If you use medication or another clinician, bring that context.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <aside>
        <div class='card'>
          <h4>Make a short plan</h4>
          <p class='note'>Build a one-paragraph plan for a first consult. Copy it and bring it to your appointment.</p>
          <textarea id='onepara' rows='6' style='width:100%;padding:10px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid #eee' placeholder='I want to work on...'></textarea>
          <div style='display:flex;gap:8px;margin-top:10px'>
            <button id='saveOne' class='primary' style='background:var(--accent);color:white;border:0;padding:10px;border-radius:8px;cursor:pointer'>Create paragraph</button>
            <button id='copyOne' style='padding:10px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid #ddd;background:white;cursor:pointer'>Copy</button>
          </div>
          <pre id='oneOut' style='margin-top:12px;background:#fafafa;padding:10px;border-radius:8px;font-family:monospace;font-size:13px'>Your paragraph will appear here.</pre>
        </div>

        <div class='card' style='margin-top:16px'>
          <h4>Self-check (non-diagnostic)</h4>
          <p class='note'>A brief set of prompts to bring to a session: rate sleep, stress, and supports; or copy them as questions to discuss.</p>
          <div style='display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px'>
            <label class='note'>Sleep (1–5)</label>
            <input id='sleep' placeholder='e.g., 3'>
            <label class='note'>Stress level (1–5)</label>
            <input id='stress' placeholder='e.g., 4'>
            <label class='note'>Main support persons</label>
            <input id='supports' placeholder='Names or descriptions'>
            <div style='display:flex;gap:8px;margin-top:8px'>
              <button id='genCheck' style='padding:8px;border-radius:8px;background:#eaf6ef;border:0;cursor:pointer'>Generate prompts</button>
              <button id='copyCheck' style='padding:8px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid #ddd;background:white;cursor:pointer'>Copy</button>
            </div>
          </div>
